-- cmd: repl
-- stdin: import string\nlet s = "one \{- two\nthree"\ns\nprintln("{string.length("(\{-")}")\n:quit\n
-- A string that spans lines and holds `{-` is a string, not the start
-- of a comment; and a string inside a string interpolation that holds
-- `(` and `{-` opens neither a paren nor a comment: the input is read
-- at once, from its tokens.
